{"kind":"request","text":"Probe Cloudflare's local Artifacts simulator (changelog 2026-11-16) and decide whether dap adopts it for local development and tests.\n\nCloudflare's wrangler dev, Vite plugin and Workers Vitest integration now simulate the `artifacts` binding locally by default. Local repos stay separate from deployed ones, and `remote = true` keeps the deployed namespace. See https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-11-16-local-artifacts-development/ and the Local development guide it links.\n\nWhat dap does today:\n- Six Wrangler configs under apps/room (wrangler.jsonc, .demo, .grow, .lending, .commons, .artroom-scope) set `\"remote\": true`. A local `wrangler dev` run against them writes to the live namespaces.\n- The tests never use the real binding. `packages/scope/test/hosts.ts` is a hand-built host stand-in, and apps/room/lanes/wrangler.test.jsonc declares no `artifacts` entry.\n- dap calls only `get`, `create` and `delete` on the binding (ArtifactsNamespace in packages/scope/src/artifacts-host.ts).\n- docs/self-host-cloudflare.md line 71 tells self-hosters that `remote: true` makes local development use the live binding.","body":{"conditions":"1. Probe from a scratch directory with a pinned recent wrangler (for example npx wrangler@\u003cversion\u003e in /tmp). Never install a package in a checkout. Read the Local development guide first and record the wrangler version and Git version used. 2. Run create, get and delete against the local simulator. Record whether it matches the production behavior dap relies on: the single-use write token that dap revokes, ALREADY_EXISTS on a taken name, the delete result (true or false), and any pack-size or read bound. 3. Clone and push through ArtifactsProvider over the local remote URL with a standard Git client. 4. Check whether @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers 0.22.0 (the pin in apps/room/lanes, apps/room/page and packages/cli) supports the binding in wrangler.test.jsonc. 5. Land one note under notes/ with the observed results, labelled by how each was taken, and a recommendation on each of: (a) removing `remote: true` from the development path so wrangler dev stops writing to live namespaces, with the change to docs/self-host-cloudflare.md line 71; (b) one workerd scenario over the real local binding, with its measured cost against docs/testing.md and the test-overhead budget; (c) the wrangler 4.147.0 pin. State plainly if the simulator is not faithful enough. Do not change a Wrangler config, the pin or a deployed Worker in this request. Any adoption change is a separate request after the note lands.","target_head":"60223c5ca82e33dee3f6a098987eaf19cf8f52c3","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}